1
00:00:02,039 --> 00:00:07,000
seemed almost indifferent as to the effect he produced.

2
00:00:07,920 --> 00:00:12,960
At this, Snowball sprang to his feet and shouting down the sheep, who had begun

3
00:00:12,960 --> 00:00:18,800
bleating again, broke into a passionate appeal in favor of the windmill.

4
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:23,560
Until now, the animals had been about equally divided in their sympathies, but

5
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:27,640
in a moment Snowball's eloquence had carried them away.

6
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:33,279
In glowing sentences, he painted a picture of Animal Farm as it might be

7
00:00:33,279 --> 00:00:37,239
when sordid labor was lifted from the animals' backs.

8
00:00:37,239 --> 00:00:43,520
His imagination had now run far beyond chaff cutters and turnip slicers.

9
00:00:43,520 --> 00:00:49,600
"Electricity," he said, "could operate threshing machines, plows, harrows,

10
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:54,840
rollers, and reapers and binders, besides supplying every stall with its

11
00:00:54,840 --> 00:01:01,079
own electric light, hot and cold water, and an electric heater."

12
00:01:01,079 --> 00:01:05,119
By the time he had finished speaking, there was no doubt as to which way the

13
00:01:05,119 --> 00:01:07,000
vote would go.

14
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:13,600
But just at this moment, Napoleon stood up, and casting a peculiar sidelong look

15
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:20,800
at Snowball, uttered a high-pitched whimper of a kind no one had ever heard him utter before.

16
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:27,399
At this, there was a terrible baying sound outside, and nine enormous dogs,

17
00:01:27,399 --> 00:01:32,000
wearing brass-studded collars, came bounding into the barn.

18
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:36,560
They dashed straight for Snowball, who only sprang from his place just in time

19
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:39,119
to escape their snapping jaws.

20
00:01:39,119 --> 00:01:43,119
In a moment, he was out of the door, and they were after him.

21
00:01:43,119 --> 00:01:49,520
Too amazed and frightened to speak, all the animals crowded through the door to watch the chase.

22
00:01:49,520 --> 00:01:53,880
Snowball was racing across the long pasture that led to the road.

23
00:01:53,880 --> 00:01:59,520
He was running as only a pig can run, but the dogs were close on his heels.

24
00:01:59,520 --> 00:02:03,520
Suddenly, he slipped, and it seemed certain that they had him.

25
00:02:03,520 --> 00:02:06,640
Then he was up again, running faster than ever.

26
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:09,319
Then the dogs were gaining on him again.

27
00:02:09,319 --> 00:02:14,479
One of them all but closed his jaws on Snowball's tail, but Snowball whisked it

28
00:02:14,479 --> 00:02:16,760
free just [music] in time.

29
00:02:16,760 --> 00:02:21,800
Then he put on an extra spurt, and with a few inches to spare, slipped through a

30
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:26,760
hole in the hedge, and was seen no more.

31
00:02:26,760 --> 00:02:31,880
Silent and terrified, the animals crept back into the barn.

32
00:02:31,880 --> 00:02:35,000
In a moment, the dogs came bounding back.

33
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:39,159
At first, no one had been able to imagine where these creatures came from,

34
00:02:39,159 --> 00:02:42,279
but the problem was soon solved.

35
00:02:42,279 --> 00:02:48,680
They were the puppies whom Napoleon had taken away from their mothers and reared privately.

36
00:02:48,680 --> 00:02:56,479
Though not yet full-grown, they were huge dogs and as fierce-looking as wolves.

37
00:02:56,479 --> 00:02:58,800
They kept close to Napoleon.

38
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:03,279
It was noticed that they wagged their tails to him in the same way as the

39
00:03:03,279 --> 00:03:05,399
other dogs had been used to do to Mr.

40
00:03:05,399 --> 00:03:06,760
Jones.

41
00:03:06,760 --> 00:03:11,640
Napoleon, with the dogs following him, now mounted onto the raised portion of

42
00:03:11,640 --> 00:03:16,399
the floor where Major had previously stood to deliver his speech.

43
00:03:16,399 --> 00:03:22,600
He announced that from now on, the Sunday morning meetings would come to an end.

44
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:26,960
"They were unnecessary," he said, "and wasted time."

45
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:32,199
In future, all questions relating to the working of the farm would be settled by

46
00:03:32,199 --> 00:03:37,319
a special committee of pigs presided over by himself.

47
00:03:37,319 --> 00:03:43,560
These would meet in private and afterwards communicate their decisions to the others.

48
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:48,640
The animals would still assemble on Sunday mornings to salute the flag, sing

49
00:03:48,640 --> 00:03:56,399
Beasts of England, and receive their orders for the week, but there would be no more debates.

50
00:03:56,399 --> 00:04:01,159
In spite of the shock that Snowball's expulsion had given them, the animals

51
00:04:01,159 --> 00:04:04,319
were dismayed by this announcement.

52
00:04:04,319 --> 00:04:09,079
Several of them would have protested if they could have found the right arguments.

53
00:04:09,079 --> 00:04:12,159
Even Boxer was vaguely troubled.

54
00:04:12,159 --> 00:04:19,720
He set his ears back, shook his forelock several times, and tried hard to marshal his thoughts.

55
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:25,359
But in the end, he could not think of anything to say.

56
00:04:25,359 --> 00:04:30,039
Some of the pigs themselves, however, were more articulate.

57
00:04:30,039 --> 00:04:35,840
Four young porkers in the front row uttered shrill squeals of disapproval,

58
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:41,560
and all four of them sprang to their feet and began speaking at once.

59
00:04:41,560 --> 00:04:48,640
But, suddenly, the dogs sitting round Napoleon let out deep, menacing growls,

60
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:52,640
and the pigs fell silent and sat down again.

61
00:04:52,640 --> 00:05:00,000
Then, the sheep broke out into a tremendous bleating of "Four legs good, two legs bad!"
